1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,400
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,520
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:07,800
This is my brother George.
[GRUNTS]

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,320
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:13,280
And this is Daddy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,760
Peppa Pig.
[GRUNTS]

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,919
[♪♪♪]

8
00:00:17,919 --> 00:00:19,960
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

9
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,560
[BANGING, POUNDING]

10
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:23,480
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
have come to play

11
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,040
in Granny
and Grandpa's garden.

12
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,400
[CLUNKING, CLANKING]

13
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,040
What's that noise?

14
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,720
Grandpa's making something.

15
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:33,000
Hello, Peppa and George.

16
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,640
That's perfect timing.

17
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,600
[GRUNTS]
I've just finished making it.

18
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,000
And may we ask
what "it" is?

19
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,559
Hee-hee-hee.
I'll show you.

20
00:00:43,559 --> 00:00:44,720
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

21
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,400
[HISSING]

22
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:49,480
PEPPA &amp; GEORGE: Wow.
A little toy train.

23
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:53,480
It's not a toy.
This is Gertrude.

24
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:57,320
She's a miniature locomotive.
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

25
00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:00,040
But doesn't it need
railway tracks to run on?

26
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:03,839
Oh, no. I've fitted
Gertrude with car wheels,

27
00:01:03,839 --> 00:01:06,440
so she can go anywhere
she likes.

28
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,600
[GRUNTS]
Grandpa, can we
ride in Gertrude?

29
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,880
Hop aboard.

30
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:14,800
[WHISTLE BLOWS]
Full steam ahead!

31
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,479
Bye bye, Granny.
See you later.

32
00:01:17,479 --> 00:01:20,039
NARRATOR: Peppa and George love
Grandpa's little train.

33
00:01:20,039 --> 00:01:21,479
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

34
00:01:21,479 --> 00:01:24,240
♪ Grandpa's little train goes
Choo choo choo ♪

35
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,759
♪ Choo choo choo
Choo choo choo ♪

36
00:01:26,759 --> 00:01:29,440
♪ Grandpa's little train goes
Choo choo choo ♪

37
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,920
♪ All day long ♪

38
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,920
♪ And the piggies on the train
Go oink oink oink ♪

39
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:37,399
♪ Oink oink oink
Oink oink oink ♪

40
00:01:37,399 --> 00:01:40,399
♪ And the piggies on the train
Go oink oink oink ♪

41
00:01:40,399 --> 00:01:42,720
♪ All day long ♪

42
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,080
[ALL LAUGH, SNORT]

43
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,679
[HONKING]

44
00:01:45,679 --> 00:01:48,559
NARRATOR: Here is Granddad Dog
with Danny Dog.

45
00:01:48,559 --> 00:01:50,839
Hello.
Hello, Danny.

46
00:01:50,839 --> 00:01:54,479
Woof. I see you're
playing toy trains.

47
00:01:54,479 --> 00:01:57,600
Toy? Gertrude isn't a toy.

48
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:00,880
[GRUNTS]
How's your little lorry?

49
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,559
Little lorry?

50
00:02:02,559 --> 00:02:07,479
My breakdown truck
is a proper, work vehicle.

51
00:02:07,479 --> 00:02:10,519
Granddad? Can I ride
on the train?

52
00:02:10,519 --> 00:02:12,640
Hm. It's your
choice, Danny,

53
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:15,239
if you'd rather
play trains than--

54
00:02:15,239 --> 00:02:18,160
Thanks, Granddad.
[GIGGLES]

55
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,920
See you later.
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

56
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:23,480
NARRATOR: Miss Rabbit is driving
the school bus.

57
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:29,160
And to our left, we can see
some hills with trees...

58
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:30,560
[WHISTLE BLOWS]
Hello, everyone.

59
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:32,040
ALL:
Hello, Peppa.

60
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:34,000
NARRATOR:
All Peppa's friends are here.

61
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,079
Can we ride on the train?

62
00:02:36,079 --> 00:02:41,760
Um. I'm giving the children
an educational bus tour.

63
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,720
Are trains educational?
They certainly are.

64
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:50,239
Uh, hands up, all those who
want to ride on the train.

65
00:02:50,239 --> 00:02:52,160
ALL:
Me! Me! Me!

66
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:55,480
MISS RABBIT:
And hands up, all those who
want to stay on the bus.

67
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:59,679
Okay, you can all
go on the train.

68
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,440
And I'll follow
along behind.

69
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,480
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

70
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:03,959
[KIDS GIGGLING]

71
00:03:03,959 --> 00:03:06,679
♪ Grandpa's little train goes
Choo choo choo ♪

72
00:03:06,679 --> 00:03:09,359
♪ Choo choo choo
Choo choo choo ♪

73
00:03:09,359 --> 00:03:12,120
♪ Grandpa's little train goes
Choo choo choo ♪

74
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:15,079
♪ All day long ♪

75
00:03:15,079 --> 00:03:17,440
NARRATOR:
What a lot of mud.

76
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,480
We don't want
to get stuck.

77
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:21,880
Maybe we should go
a different way.

78
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,959
It's only a patch of mud.

79
00:03:23,959 --> 00:03:27,760
Come on, Gertrude.
You can make it.

80
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,840
Come on, bus.
You can make it.

81
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:32,320
[ENGINE WHIRRING]

82
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,239
NARRATOR:
The bus is stuck in the mud.

83
00:03:34,239 --> 00:03:36,519
Oh, bother.
[TRUCK HORN HONKS]

84
00:03:36,519 --> 00:03:38,600
Ruff.
Hello, Miss Rabbit.

85
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:39,799
How are you today?

86
00:03:39,799 --> 00:03:43,040
I'm a bit stuck.
Can you rescue me?

87
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,079
Certainly.

88
00:03:45,079 --> 00:03:47,560
Is your truck
strong enough?

89
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,799
Trust me.
[REVVING]

90
00:03:50,799 --> 00:03:52,079
[SPLOSHING]

91
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:56,840
Did it work?
Uh. No.

92
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:59,839
We need a vehicle
with more power.

93
00:03:59,839 --> 00:04:01,040
[TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWS]

94
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,720
Can I help in any way?

95
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,239
Uh, it's nothing that
I can't deal with.

96
00:04:05,239 --> 00:04:06,560
Thanks, anyway.

97
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,160
I've got an idea.

98
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:11,399
Grandpa Pig's train can
tow me out of the mud.

99
00:04:11,399 --> 00:04:14,679
Uh, good thinking,
Miss Rabbit.

100
00:04:14,679 --> 00:04:18,800
NARRATOR:
Grandpa's little train is going
to pull the bus out of the mud.

101
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,800
Full steam.

102
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,640
ALL:
Come on, Gertrude!

103
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,719
[STRAINING]
Come on, Gertrude!

104
00:04:25,719 --> 00:04:27,400
KIDS:
Hooray!

105
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,880
Ho ho. Well done.

106
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:32,840
It's amazing what can be
done by a toy train.

107
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:37,479
Toy? Gertrude isn't a toy.

108
00:04:37,479 --> 00:04:42,039
Gertrude is the very best train
in the whole world.

109
00:04:42,039 --> 00:04:43,400
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

110
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:45,880
[ALL LAUGH]

111
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:49,520
[♪♪♪]

112
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,719
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

113
00:04:51,719 --> 00:04:54,599
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George are visiting
their big cousin Chloé.

114
00:04:54,599 --> 00:04:57,360
[GRUNTS]
Today, as well as
seeing Chloé,

115
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,960
you are going to
meet your new cousin.

116
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,039
Ooh.

117
00:05:02,039 --> 00:05:04,880
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family have
arrived at Chloé's house.

118
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:07,200
DADDY PIG: Hello.
UNCLE PIG: Hello, everyone.

119
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,159
[GRUNTS]
Hello, Peppa and George.

120
00:05:09,159 --> 00:05:11,479
NARRATOR: This is Chloé,
Peppa and George's big cousin.

121
00:05:11,479 --> 00:05:13,840
[SNORTS]
But where's
our new cousin?

122
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:15,680
Here's your
new baby cousin.

123
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:17,479
Ooh.

124
00:05:17,479 --> 00:05:20,400
NARRATOR: The new cousin
is a tiny, baby piggy.

125
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,240
Goo, goo, goo.
[GRUNTS]

126
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:24,960
Oh, how beautiful.

127
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,680
Is it a girl baby?

128
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:29,440
No, it's a boy.
Oh.

129
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:31,080
I wish it was a girl.
Me too.

130
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:32,719
[GRUNTS, GIGGLES]

131
00:05:32,719 --> 00:05:34,800
NARRATOR: George is pleased
the baby is a boy.

132
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:38,520
Dine-Saw. Grrrr.
[CRYING]

133
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:42,039
[GRUNTS]
I think the baby's too little
to play with dinosaurs.

134
00:05:42,039 --> 00:05:45,359
George, the baby doesn't
want to play with you.

135
00:05:45,359 --> 00:05:47,760
It wants to play
with me.

136
00:05:49,039 --> 00:05:50,599
[CRYING]

137
00:05:50,599 --> 00:05:54,440
Peppa, the baby is much too
little to play ball games.

138
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:57,039
But if it can't play
with a dinosaur,

139
00:05:57,039 --> 00:05:59,680
or a ball,
what can it do?

140
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,479
It eats
and it sleeps.

141
00:06:01,479 --> 00:06:03,800
[BURPS]
And it does that.

142
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,359
[ALL LAUGH]

143
00:06:05,359 --> 00:06:08,520
[GRUNTS]
Aunty Pig,
can I hold the baby?

144
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:12,680
Yes. If you're very careful,
you can hold Alexander.

145
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:15,560
Alexander?
AUNTY PIG: That's his name.

146
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,520
Baby Alexander.

147
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:20,200
NARRATOR: What a big name
for such a small piggy.

148
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:23,840
It's quite nice,
even though it's a boy.

149
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,960
Goo, goo, goo.

150
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:28,799
Oh. What's that smell?

151
00:06:28,799 --> 00:06:32,320
Maybe Alexander's
nappy needs changing.

152
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,680
Ew. Disgusting.

153
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:38,440
Peppa, when you were
a baby, you wore nappies.

154
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,080
I did not.

155
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:41,719
[ALL LAUGHING]

156
00:06:41,719 --> 00:06:44,719
Mommy, can I play with Peppa
and George in the garden?

157
00:06:44,719 --> 00:06:46,840
[GRUNTS]
Yes.

158
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:50,599
[KIDS GIGGLING]

159
00:06:50,599 --> 00:06:54,080
Chloé, is it nice having
a little baby brother?

160
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,640
Yes. Alexander
is very sweet.

161
00:06:56,640 --> 00:07:00,080
[GRUNTS]
I wish George was a sweet,
little baby piggy.

162
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,280
I know.

163
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:04,719
George can pretend
to be a baby piggy.

164
00:07:04,719 --> 00:07:06,400
He can go in my doll's pram.

165
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,799
That's a good idea.
No.

166
00:07:08,799 --> 00:07:11,039
NARRATOR: George does not want
to be a baby.

167
00:07:11,039 --> 00:07:14,200
George, if you pretend
to be a baby,

168
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:18,400
I promise to be nice
to you forever and ever.

169
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,880
NARRATOR:
George is thinking.

170
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:22,239
And you can play
with all my toys.

171
00:07:22,239 --> 00:07:23,880
NARRATOR:
George is thinking more.

172
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:27,080
And when we get home, you
can play with all my toys.

173
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:30,640
[GRUNTS, GIGGLES]
NARRATOR: George has decided.

174
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:33,239
What a sweet baby piggy.
[GIGGLES]

175
00:07:33,239 --> 00:07:35,239
[BELLS RINGING]

176
00:07:35,239 --> 00:07:39,200
NARRATOR:
Here are Candy Cat, Suzy Sheep,
Rebecca Rabbit and Zoe Zebra.

177
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,599
ALL:
Hello.

178
00:07:40,599 --> 00:07:44,640
Baa. Why is George
in that doll's pram?

179
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:48,000
It's not George.
It's a baby piggy.

180
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,520
Goo, goo.
But it is George.

181
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:53,479
George is a pretend
baby piggy.

182
00:07:53,479 --> 00:07:54,919
ALL: Ah!

183
00:07:54,919 --> 00:07:56,680
Is it a girl or a boy?

184
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,919
It's a girl.
No.

185
00:07:58,919 --> 00:08:01,719
NARRATOR:
George does not want
to be a girl baby.

186
00:08:01,719 --> 00:08:04,599
Okay. It's a boy.
[CHUCKLES]

187
00:08:04,599 --> 00:08:06,719
I've got some cookies.

188
00:08:06,719 --> 00:08:09,000
Would the baby piggy
like one?

189
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:13,200
Oh, no. It can't eat cookies.
[CRYING]

190
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,960
NARRATOR:
George likes cookies.

191
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:17,479
Maybe it can have
one cookie.

192
00:08:17,479 --> 00:08:20,039
[LAUGHS]
Goo, goo.

193
00:08:20,039 --> 00:08:21,880
It's so clever.

194
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:24,719
And so handsome.
[BURPS]

195
00:08:24,719 --> 00:08:25,919
[ALL LAUGH]

196
00:08:25,919 --> 00:08:27,400
It's very funny.

197
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,560
It's the best
baby piggy ever.

198
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,520
NARRATOR:
George likes this game.

199
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:37,400
Here is Aunty Pig,
with Baby Alexander.

200
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:41,159
Wow.
A proper, real baby piggy.

201
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,640
It's so gorgeous.

202
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,280
It's much sweeter
than George.

203
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:49,840
[SOBS]
NARRATOR: Oh, dear.

204
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,760
George liked being
the baby piggy.

205
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:56,040
Oh, George. You'll always be
my baby piggy.

206
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,280
[WHIMPERS]

207
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,360
Maybe it's time
for a new game.

208
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:02,280
How about some
dinosaur chasing?

209
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:04,760
[GIGGLES]
Grrr.

210
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:07,840
ALL:
Eek! Too scary!

211
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,400
Grrr.

212
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,319
NARRATOR: George liked being
a baby piggy,

213
00:09:11,319 --> 00:09:14,120
but he likes being
George more.

214
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,880
[ALL LAUGH]

215
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,199
[♪♪♪]

216
00:09:19,199 --> 00:09:21,400
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

217
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,600
NARRATOR:
It is a lovely sunny day.

218
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:26,000
Peppa and George are
finishing their breakfast.

219
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,800
[GRUNTS]
Today is a good day
for a cycle ride.

220
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:32,720
A cycle ride. Yippee!
[GRUNTS]

221
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:35,560
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
love cycle rides.

222
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:37,439
Peppa has her bicycle.

223
00:09:37,439 --> 00:09:38,720
[RINGS BELL]

224
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,319
George has his tricycle.

225
00:09:40,319 --> 00:09:41,880
[RINGS BELL]

226
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:44,319
Mommy and Daddy
have their tandem.

227
00:09:44,319 --> 00:09:47,480
What's that?
It's our bicycle.

228
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:49,240
[HONKS HORN]
[BOTH GIGGLE]

229
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:52,760
I sit at the front and
Mommy Pig sits at the back.

230
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,600
[GRUNTS]
And we can put these
two seats on the back

231
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,240
for Peppa and George.

232
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:00,839
But we want to ride
our own bicycles.

233
00:10:00,839 --> 00:10:04,319
George is a bit too little,
his legs will get very tired.

234
00:10:04,319 --> 00:10:07,959
But I'm a big girl,
I won't get tired.

235
00:10:07,959 --> 00:10:11,240
It will be a long cycle ride,
Peppa. Are you sure?

236
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:13,400
Yes, Daddy, I'm sure.

237
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,520
Okay.
Are we all ready?

238
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,959
Yes, Daddy Pig.

239
00:10:16,959 --> 00:10:18,720
Then let's go.

240
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,439
[BIKE HORN HONKS]
Whee!

241
00:10:20,439 --> 00:10:22,120
I'm winning.

242
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:26,160
It's not a race, Peppa,
it's just a gentle bicycle ride.

243
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:31,360
Yes, Daddy,
but I'm still winning.

244
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:34,400
[RINGS BIKE BELL]
[PANTING]

245
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:37,880
Ha-ha-ha.
Now we're winning.

246
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:40,160
[BLOWS RASPBERRY, GIGGLES]

247
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:44,360
I don't like cycling uphill.
[PANTS]

248
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:46,640
Peppa, we won the race.

249
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:49,199
[PANTING]
No, you didn't, Daddy.

250
00:10:49,199 --> 00:10:52,360
Because I wasn't racing
that time.

251
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,319
But now I am.
[GIGGLES]

252
00:10:54,319 --> 00:10:56,640
Can't catch me.
[SNORTS]

253
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:59,280
Ha, ha.
You cheeky little piggy.

254
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:00,800
[RINGS BELL]
[LAUGHING]

255
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:04,160
Hello, ducks.
We're having a cycle ride.

256
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:05,959
[BIKE HORN HONKS]
[QUACKING]

257
00:11:05,959 --> 00:11:07,439
Hello, ducks!
[HORN HONKS]

258
00:11:07,439 --> 00:11:08,800
[ALL QUACKING]

259
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:14,400
Ah, I'd forgotten how
much I love cycling.

260
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:20,040
Oh, I'd forgotten how much
I hate cycling up hills.

261
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:22,400
NARRATOR: The ground
is getting quite steep.

262
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:26,280
Ugh. I don't like
cycling up hills.

263
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:30,319
But look at the beautiful view.

264
00:11:30,319 --> 00:11:33,000
[STRAINING]
My... goodness,

265
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,839
this... is...
hard work.

266
00:11:36,839 --> 00:11:39,319
Mommy Pig.
You're not pedaling.

267
00:11:39,319 --> 00:11:41,079
Oh. Sorry, Daddy Pig,

268
00:11:41,079 --> 00:11:44,319
I was just enjoying the view.
[ALL GIGGLE]

269
00:11:44,319 --> 00:11:47,480
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family have
reached the top of the hill.

270
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,800
[KIDS GIGGLING]

271
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:50,680
NARRATOR:
All Peppa's friends are here.

272
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:52,160
ALL: Hello, Peppa.
Hello.

273
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,880
Woof. We're going to have
a race on our bikes.

274
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:58,000
Baa. Peppa, do you
want to race too?

275
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,240
[GRUNTS]
Okay, as long as we can
race down hill.

276
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:04,680
Okay.
[KIDS LAUGH]

277
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:07,640
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends are
going to race down the hill.

278
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:08,800
[GRUNTS]
Are you all ready?

279
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:10,079
ALL:
Ready!

280
00:12:10,079 --> 00:12:13,000
You can start,
when I honk the horn.

281
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,719
Like this...
[HONKS HORN]

282
00:12:14,719 --> 00:12:16,880
NARRATOR:
Pedro has set off too soon.

283
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:20,319
Stop, Pedro!
The race hasn't started yet!

284
00:12:21,439 --> 00:12:23,079
Sorry, Mr. Pig.

285
00:12:23,079 --> 00:12:27,640
I was just letting you know that
the horn sounded like this...

286
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:29,000
[HONKS HORN]
Whee!

287
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,760
ALL:
Stop! Stop!

288
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:34,920
Sorry, Pedro, that time
it was my fault.

289
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:38,839
The next time I honk the horn...
you can go.

290
00:12:38,839 --> 00:12:41,480
Did he say go?
I think so.

291
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:43,360
ALL:
Go! Go! Go!

292
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,599
Go on, Peppa.

293
00:12:44,599 --> 00:12:47,880
But, Daddy, you didn't
honk the horn.

294
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:49,680
[HONKS HORN]

295
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:51,839
NARRATOR:
Danny Dog is in the lead.

296
00:12:51,839 --> 00:12:54,000
Wait for me.
[RINGS BELL]

297
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,079
Whee!

298
00:12:56,079 --> 00:12:58,439
I win.
[GRUNTS]

299
00:12:58,439 --> 00:12:59,839
ALL:
Well done, Peppa!

300
00:12:59,839 --> 00:13:03,560
Yes. I'm very good
at cycling downhill.

301
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:05,120
[ALL LAUGHING]

302
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,400
NARRATOR:
It is home time
for Peppa's friends.

303
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,959
Bye bye, Peppa.

304
00:13:08,959 --> 00:13:10,319
Bye.

305
00:13:10,319 --> 00:13:12,280
Home time for
us too, Peppa.

306
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:15,079
Mommy. I'm tired.

307
00:13:15,079 --> 00:13:20,880
[GRUNTS]
All this cycling up and down
hills has made my legs tired.

308
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:22,760
Can I ride
on your bike?

309
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:25,040
But where will
Daddy Pig sit?

310
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:30,040
Um... Daddy can ride my bike,
it's very nice.

311
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:32,319
Oh. Okay.

312
00:13:34,319 --> 00:13:35,760
[HONKS HORN]

313
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:38,240
[GIGGLES]
I love the tandem.

314
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:40,719
[GRUNTS]
Daddy, do you like my bike?

315
00:13:40,719 --> 00:13:44,120
Yes, Peppa,
it's very nice.

316
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:47,880
[ALL LAUGH]

317
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,120
[GIGGLING]

318
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,079
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

319
00:13:52,079 --> 00:13:55,560
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George are in Granny
and Grandpa Pig's garden.

320
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:59,120
They're going to play
in their treehouse.

321
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,280
Peppa and George
love their treehouse.

322
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:03,480
[BELL RINGS]

323
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,439
NARRATOR: Here are Peppa
and George's friends--

324
00:14:05,439 --> 00:14:09,599
Zoe, Suzy,
Rebecca and Richard.

325
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:12,599
Baa. I like
your treehouse, Peppa.

326
00:14:12,599 --> 00:14:15,400
Can we come in?
Yes.

327
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:18,680
[SNORTS]
Now we can have a tea party.

328
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:20,280
[ALL LAUGH]

329
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,520
[BELL RINGS]

330
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:25,040
NARRATOR:
Here are Pedro and Danny.

331
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:28,479
Neigh. Hello, Peppa.
Woof. Can we come in?

332
00:14:28,479 --> 00:14:32,439
Sorry, Danny. Only girls can
come into the treehouse.

333
00:14:32,439 --> 00:14:34,880
Boys are a bit noisy.

334
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,680
They always spoil
the tea parties.

335
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:40,040
But George and
Richard are boys.

336
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:43,880
[GIGGLING]
Oh. Yes.

337
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,599
Sorry, George.

338
00:14:45,599 --> 00:14:49,760
This treehouse
is for girls only.

339
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:54,079
[BOTH CRY]

340
00:14:54,079 --> 00:14:55,439
What's wrong?

341
00:14:55,439 --> 00:14:58,560
The girls won't let us
into the treehouse.

342
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:00,199
Woof. It isn't fair.

343
00:15:00,199 --> 00:15:03,199
Ho. Ho.
I think I can help.

344
00:15:03,199 --> 00:15:04,920
Come over here.

345
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:11,760
Now we can have a nice,
quiet tea party.

346
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:14,880
[BANGING]
What's that noise?

347
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:16,240
[HAMMERING]

348
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:18,040
[♪♪♪]

349
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:20,479
There. Now you boys

350
00:15:20,479 --> 00:15:26,120
have your very own den with
its very own drawbridge.

351
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:29,280
A castle!
Thank you, Grandpa Pig.

352
00:15:33,319 --> 00:15:35,120
[SNORTS]
Can we come in?

353
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:39,079
No. This is a boys' den.
For boys only.

354
00:15:39,079 --> 00:15:41,280
[GRINDING]

355
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,520
But I love castles.

356
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:46,880
Castles aren't as good
as treehouses.

357
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:49,000
[GRUNTS]
Come on, girls.

358
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,280
♪ I'm the king of the castle ♪

359
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:52,400
[LAUGHS]

360
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:55,719
Every castle
needs a flag.

361
00:15:55,719 --> 00:15:57,160
BOYS:
Wow.

362
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:59,319
They've got a flag.

363
00:15:59,319 --> 00:16:01,959
We don't need a silly flag.

364
00:16:01,959 --> 00:16:03,959
NARRATOR:
Here is Granny Pig.

365
00:16:03,959 --> 00:16:06,400
Hello, girls.
Can I get you anything?

366
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,920
GIRLS:
A flag, please.

367
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:11,359
And it must be better
than the boys' flag.

368
00:16:11,359 --> 00:16:12,920
I'll see what I can do.

369
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:15,479
♪ I'm the king of the castle ♪

370
00:16:15,479 --> 00:16:19,560
Ho. Ho. Every castle
needs a telephone.

371
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:21,040
[GRUNTS]
Hold this.

372
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,359
[♪♪♪]

373
00:16:22,359 --> 00:16:24,640
Keep this string
nice and tight,

374
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,880
and you can talk
to the boys.

375
00:16:28,479 --> 00:16:31,319
We don't want to
talk to the boys.

376
00:16:31,319 --> 00:16:34,839
We don't want to talk
to the girls.

377
00:16:34,839 --> 00:16:36,920
[BLOWS RASPBERRY]

378
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,079
[BLOWS RASPBERRY]

379
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:42,800
NARRATOR: Granny Pig has found
a flag for the girls' den.

380
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,839
This dress will make
a pretty flag.

381
00:16:44,839 --> 00:16:47,760
[GRUNTS]
Thank you, Granny.

382
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:50,880
It isn't as good as
the boys' flag.

383
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,880
I wish we were in
the castle.

384
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:56,000
Fairy princesses
live in castles.

385
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:00,680
If I were a fairy princess,
I would live in a treehouse.

386
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:04,159
Can we come over?
Please?

387
00:17:04,159 --> 00:17:08,960
Only if you say
the castle is the best.

388
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:11,760
It is the best.
[GIRLS GIGGLE]

389
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:14,560
I'm staying in
my treehouse.

390
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:17,159
[BRIDGE WHIRRING]
[KIDS GIGGLE]

391
00:17:17,159 --> 00:17:21,960
Baa. I love the castle.
[ALL GIGGLE]

392
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:26,119
NARRATOR:
Oh dear, it is raining,
and the castle has no roof.

393
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:30,440
Let's go to
the treehouse.

394
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:33,120
No. I'll never
leave my castle.

395
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:36,320
Squeak.
Neigh.
Baa.

396
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:38,240
[ALL LAUGHING]

397
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:43,440
NARRATOR:
The rain has stopped.

398
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:46,720
[GRUNTS, GIGGLES]

399
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:48,960
NARRATOR: George has found
a muddy puddle.

400
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:51,800
That looks fun.

401
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:55,040
[ALL LAUGHING]

402
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:57,200
I'm staying in my castle.

403
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,720
I'm staying in my treehouse.

404
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:04,080
Ho, ho. I'll look after
your castle, Danny.

405
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:06,600
I'll look after your
treehouse, Peppa.

406
00:18:08,639 --> 00:18:12,760
NARRATOR:
Peppa and Danny love jumping up
and down in muddy puddles.

407
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:15,879
Everyone loves jumping up
and down in muddy puddles,

408
00:18:15,879 --> 00:18:18,760
whether they are
girls or boys.

409
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,200
[♪♪♪]

410
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,280
[GIGGLING, GRUNTING]

411
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,879
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

412
00:18:22,879 --> 00:18:25,760
[SNORTING, LAUGHING]

413
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,840
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

414
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:30,159
[GRUNTING, GIGGLING]

415
00:18:30,159 --> 00:18:31,639
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

416
00:18:31,639 --> 00:18:33,600
[SNORTING]

